<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan central bank accepts 5.7 bln bonds in OMO.</title>
<headline>Pakistan central bank accepts 5.7 bln bonds in OMO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Sunday it had sold 5.7 billion rupees of six-month federal bonds in a special open market operation.</p>
<p>Bracketed figures show results of the last special open market operations on August 25.</p>
<p>		    Offered	  Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p>Outright sales 4,200 (3,450)  4,200 (100)   13.24 pct/yr (13.20)</p>
<p>5-month REPO   1,200	    1,200	   13.00 pct/yr</p>
<p>3-month REPO    nil		nil	     ----------</p>
<p>One-month REPO   300	     300	   12.30 pct/yr</p>
<p>Total</p>
<p>(million rupees)   5,700	    5,700</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
